{"author":{"id":"127a58c7f014820991be95805df42525db12c92e2d7319d04d4df105a9aa3444"},"ops":[{"type":1,"timestamp":1788350813,"nonce":"cQsyhxFHgKjELstwi2ooGY4QdWI=","title":"Run `m1-20260901`: rooms silently disappeared from `temperature.rooms` as their contents burned. Room 52 (Laboratory) was gone by day 40; room 54 (Kitchen) by day 50. The agent never learned that it had lost a laboratory or a kitchen — the rows simply stopped being printed, which is indistinguishable from a room the agent never had.","message":"A building being destroyed, or a room losing the role it was built for, is a structural regression. Nothing in the observation surface reports one.\n\n\n1. A room whose `role` changes away from a previously observed role is reported, naming the old role, the new role, and the tick of the change.\n2. A destroyed player-built building of consequence (a bench, a bed, a cooler, a heater, a door, a wall belonging to a placed layout) produces a report the agent can read at its next turn, not only a journal row it had to be watching for.\n3. `checklists/triggered.md` gains the act-keyed line, and the fire path in particular: after any fire, confirm the rooms that existed before it still exist with their roles.\n4. `accept/\u003cid\u003e-lost-room.py` on a bench: build a room with a role, destroy its role-defining contents, assert the regression is reported rather than the row vanishing.\n\n\n**Room identity is not stable.** `Verse.Room.ID` is assigned on rebuild, and `Map.MapUpdate` calls `TryRebuildDirtyRegionsAndRooms` every frame, so \"room 52\" is not the same handle across days and a naive diff on room id will report churn as loss. Before writing anything, establish against the decompiled source what a durable room handle actually is — candidates are the role-defining building's `thingIDNumber`, the layout id the room was placed from, or a cell that is known to be inside it.\n\n**If no durable handle exists that does not require the mod to invent and persist 